AcquisitionMethod: data-dependent MS/MS
AlkylationReagent: chloroacetamide
CleavageAgent: trypsin
CleavageAgent: Lys-C
CollisionEnergy: 30-40% normalized collision energy
Disease: Alzheimer disease (AD)
Disease: sporadic AD
FactorValue: sporadic AD
FactorValue: control
FlowRateChromatogram: 250 nl/min
FractionationMethod: pre-fractionated into 72 fractions using HiRIEF with the broad range pH 3-10 IPG drystrip
FragmentMassTolerance: fragment ion mass tolerance of 0.02 Da
FragmentationMethod: higher energy collision dissociation
Instrument: hybrid Q-Exactive-HF mass spectrometer (Thermo Scientific)
Label: TMT10plex 126-131Da
Label: amine-reactive isobaric tandem mass tags (TMTs)
MaterialType: tissue
Modification: carbamidomethylation on cysteine residues
Modification: oxidation on methionine residues
Modification: TMT10plex on peptide N termini
Modification: lysine residues
NumberOfBiologicalReplicates: 10
NumberOfFractions: 72 contiguous fractions
NumberOfMissedCleavages: 2 missed cleavages
NumberOfSamples: ten samples
NumberOfTechnicalReplicates: No technical replicates
Organism: human
OrganismPart: outer two-thirds of the molecular layer of the dentate gyrus
OrganismPart: frozen hippocampal tissues
PooledSample: pooled
PrecursorMassTolerance: precursor mass tolerance of 10 ppm
ReductionReagent: DTT
Separation: Samples were trapped on a C18 guard-desalting column (Acclaim PepMap 100, 75 mum x 2 cm, nanoViper, C18, 5 mum, 100Ang), and separated on a 50 cm long C18 column (Easy spray PepMap RSLC, C18, 2 mum, 100Ang, 75 mum x 50 cm).
